{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We have a problem: count binary words of length 12 that do not contain any forbidden substring: \"111\" or \"000\". So we need to count number of binary strings of length 12 with no run of 3 consecutive identical bits. Equivalent to avoid 000 and 111. This is a classic combinatorics / automaton counting problem. We can use recurrence or dynamic programming. Let's compute.\n\nWe can model as a finite automaton with states representing last two bits (or last run length). Since we need to avoid 3 consecutive same bits, we can keep track of last two bits or last run length. Let's define DP[n][k][b] where n length processed, k is length of current run of same bit (1 or 2), b is current bit (0 or 1). But we can also use simpler: DP[n][state] where state is last two bits pattern? Let's do run length approach.\n\nLet a_n be number of strings of length n ending with a run of length 1 (i.e., last bit differs from previous bit). Let b_n be number ending with run length 2 (i.e., last two bits same, but third last different). For n=1: a_1 = 2 (strings \"0\", \"1\") because run length 1. b_1 = 0.\n\nTransition: For next bit, if we are in state a_n (run length 1), we can add same bit -> run length becomes 2 (b_{n+1} += a_n). Or add different bit -> run length 1 (a_{n+1} += a_n). If we are in state b_n (run length 2), we cannot add same bit because that would make run length 3 forbidden. So we must add different bit -> run length 1 (a_{n+1} += b_n). So recurrence:\n\na_{n+1} = a_n + b_n\nb_{n+1} = a_n\n\nwith initial a_1=2, b_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=12.\n\nLet's compute iteratively.\n\nn=1: a=2, b=0\nn=2: a2 = a1 + b1 = 2+0=2; b2 = a1 = 2\nn=3: a3 = a2 + b2 = 2+2=4; b3 = a2 = 2\nn=4: a4 = a3 + b3 = 4+2=6; b4 = a3 = 4\nn=5: a5 = a4 + b4 = 6+4=10; b5 = a4 = 6\nn=6: a6 = a5 + b5 = 10+6=16; b6 = a5 = 10\nn=7: a7 = a6 + b6 = 16+10=26; b7 = a6 = 16\nn=8: a8 = a7 + b7 = 26+16=42; b8 = a7 = 26\nn=9: a9 = a8 + b8 = 42+26=68; b9 = a8 = 42\nn=10: a10 = a9 + b9 = 68+42=110; b10 = a9 = 68\nn=11: a11 = a10 + b10 = 110+68=178; b11 = a10 = 110\nn=12: a12 = a11 + b11 = 178+110=288; b12"}}],"created":1790984627,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3713,"total_tokens":4481,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-g4uWfWHSil1z4DFK9o0m40m5v7OAzj0y","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3713,"prompt_ms":456.144,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.1228505251817937,"prompt_per_second":8139.973341751727,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2360.866,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.078052151238592,"predicted_per_second":324.88078527116744}}